@cooked
on-arrival: dnvp_party_leader = "Alfred Hugenberg"; dnvp_ideology = "National Conservatism (Hugenbergite)"; old_middle_dnvp += 5; rural_dnvp += 3; workers_dnvp -= 3; new_middle_dnvp -= 5; pro_republic -= 5; nationalism += 5; dnvp_relation -= 20; lmabach_stage = -1

= Lambach has been defeated in the vote of no confidence!

The tally is announced to a hushed congress floor. Alfred Hugenberg has exploited the instability amongst Traditionalists and with the assistance of anti Lambach oriented Traditionalists, has easily ousted Walther Lambach from his position, unquestionably solidifying his position as new chairman.

Walther Lambach, disheartened by this event, has gathered everyone from People's Conservative group and some Moderates to challenge Hugenberg last time...

@survives
on-arrival: lambach_stage = 1; workers_dnvp += 3; new_middle_dnvp += 3 {!
Q.dnf_flee_timer = 6;
!}

= Lambach survives the vote of no confidence!

To the shock of the hall, Walther Lambach, alien to the DNVP person has survived the vote of no confidence and utilizing this fact, begun expelling dissident groups from his party and branches, although some branches show disobedience, disbanding which could have electorally bad impact on party.

On the other side, Alfred Hugenberg had gathered his people and understanding that the situation has reached it's end, initiated plans to split away from DNVP to form his own radical nationalist organization, **DNF** (Deutschenationale Front).

His survival has further caused more earthquakes inside the party, forcing Traditionalists and Moderates to turn against him and there are even rumors that second vote of no confidence will be launched...
